implementationPlan.description:
Create `RunDAG` wrapper component in `dashboard/src/components/workflows/dag/RunDAG.tsx`.

**Purpose:** The main DAG visualizer component used by WorkflowDetailPage.

**Props:**
```ts
interface RunDAGProps {
  workflow: Workflow;
  run?: WorkflowRun | null;
  onNodeClick?: (stepId: string) => void;
  className?: string;
}
```

**Implementation:**
- Calls `buildRunGraph(workflow, run)` to get nodes/edges
- Registers `nodeTypes = { runOverlay: RunOverlayNode }` (memoized outside component)
- Renders `<ReactFlow>` with:
  - `fitView`, `nodesDraggable={false}`, `nodesConnectable={false}`
  - Background dots, MiniMap, Controls
  - `onNodeClick` → extract stepId from node, call `props.onNodeClick`
- Memoize nodes/edges with `useMemo` keyed on `[workflow.steps, run?.id, run?.updatedAt]`

**SECURITY:** `onNodeClick` only passes string stepId (not full node data). ReactFlow interactions are read-only (no editing).

Create barrel export `dashboard/src/components/workflows/dag/index.ts` and verify TypeScript compilation.

**Exports:**
```ts
export { RunOverlayNode } from './RunOverlayNode';
export { RunDAG } from './RunDAG';
export { buildRunGraph } from './buildRunGraph';
export { markCriticalPath, colorEdgesByStatus } from './dagStyles';
```

**Verification:** Run `node ./node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit` to ensure all types resolve and no errors.

**Also add CSS for pulse animation** if not already in Tailwind config — check if `animate-pulse` is sufficient or if a custom `@keyframes dagPulse` is needed for the amber approval node.
